Job Title: Media Buyer
Company: WPP Media South Africa
Location: Johannesburg, South Africa
Reports To: Client Lead

Purpose: The Media Buyer is responsible for effective negotiating, purchasing/booking and administration of time or space that is acquired across all media touch points on behalf of the client. The Buyer is responsible for ensuring the media appears on-time at the best cost whilst being accountable for managing all investment.&nbsp;

Buying/Booking
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Take responsibility for administration related to transactions with media owners, including providing relevant documentation i.e. applications/booking instructions, contracts, and confirmation instructions.&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Provide accurate and detailed information on the CI to the media owner and advise the various media owners of the creative agency supplying the material.&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Notify the team of unavailable spots/positions and suitable alternatives.&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Issue accurate and detailed material chase lists for all mediums to creative agencies.&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Digitally file bookings and related correspondence to be accurate, timeous, and logical.&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Create IO’s in Symphony to buy/bill Digital media.&nbsp;

Negotiation&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Negotiate over and above the Planners’ schedule for best deals possible. This includes negotiation of additional discounts at time of booking or placing of advertising in a better position.&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Negotiate compensation for non-placement and incorrect media placement.&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Every media placement booked should carry a discount or added value.&nbsp;

Billings
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Input data into the media administrative system for billing and budget control purposes.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Ensure all rate stages, dates and positions are correct and loaded onto the billing system accordingly i.e., rate card rate, discount, net, AV, special loading, etc.&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Continuously inform the relevant stakeholder of any rate, position, or date changes.&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;All media to be loaded and checked against media contracts and schedules.&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Balance flow plans with actual monthly expenditure.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Co-ordinate with the finance department to ensure billing ensues correctly and timeously.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Update flowplans to accompany the client’s monthly statements &amp; invoices.&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Run monthly reports to assist Planners with updating flow plans, Schedules &amp; PO Trackers.&nbsp;

Other&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Supply tear sheets to clients on any print bookings.&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Supply site bibles to client for OOH.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Supply media costs on request.&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Maintain good media owner relationships.&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Assist on financial queries and the timeous resolution thereof.&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Assist in new vendor onboarding through ME-Suite &nbsp;

The Ideal Candidate &nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Minimum 4 years’ work experience in a Buying role.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Experience working at a Media Agency preferable.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Strong understanding of the media landscape.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Significant proven experience of working with multiple stakeholders, e.g., suppliers, advertising/marketing agencies, media owners. &nbsp;
